thig14.1:6.1 starts: A sweetness they exude everywhere,
thig14.1:6.2 starts: the trees risen-up with their pollen.
thig14.1:6.3 starts: The beginning of spring is a pleasant season—
thig14.1:6.4 starts: Come, let’s delight in the flowering grove.
thig14.1:9.1 starts: Like a doll made of gold, you will
thig14.1:9.2 starts: like a goddess in the gardens of heaven.
thig14.1:9.3 starts: With delicate, smooth Kāsī fabrics,
thig14.1:9.4 starts: you will shine, O beauty without compare.
thig14.1:13.1 starts: Climb onto a costly bed,
thig14.1:13.2 starts: scented with sandalwood carvings,
thig14.1:13.3 starts: with a well-washed coverlet, beautiful,
thig14.1:13.4 starts: spread with a woolen quilt, brand new.
thig14.1:14.1 starts: Like a blue lotus rising from the water
thig14.1:14.2 starts: where no human beings dwell,
thig14.1:14.3 starts: you will go to old age with your
thig14.1:14.4 starts: if you stay as you are in the
thig14.1:22.1 starts: Try to seduce one who hasn’t reflected on
thig14.1:22.2 starts: or who has not followed the Master’s teaching.
thig14.1:22.3 starts: But try it with this one who knows
thig14.1:22.4 starts: and you suffer.
thig14.1:29.1 starts: Like an evaporated mirage,
thig14.1:29.2 starts: like a tree of gold in a dream,
thig14.1:29.3 starts: like a magic show in the midst of
thig14.1:29.4 starts: you run blind after what is unreal.
ud2.3:3.1 starts: Whoever hits with a stick
ud2.3:3.2 starts: beings desiring ease,
ud2.3:3.3 starts: when he himself is looking for ease,
ud2.3:3.4 starts: will meet with no ease after death.
ud2.3:4.1 starts: Whoever doesn’t hit with a stick
ud2.3:4.2 starts: beings desiring ease,
ud2.3:4.3 starts: when he himself is looking for ease,
ud2.3:4.4 starts: will meet with ease after death.
thig14.1:3.1 starts: I respect the Master’s message,
thig14.1:3.2 starts: the training pointed out by the One Well-Gone.
thig14.1:3.3 starts: I am pure, without blemish:
thig14.1:3.4 starts: Why do you stand in my way?
ud2.7:5.1 starts: Tied down by the allure
ud2.7:5.2 starts: hosts of devas, most human beings,
ud2.7:5.3 starts: worn out with misery,
ud2.7:5.4 starts: fall under the sway
